    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A rich 1920s Mexico City socialite trapped in an arranged marriage she despised, Caridad poisoned her husband, was caught, and was Embraced by Donna Fería on the eve of her hanging. She grew into a scholar of the Path of Cathari and abyss mysticism, identifying with Persephone, and now serves the Partido Devolucionario Institucional as pack priest while supplying the drug kalif (cannabis fed on vitae) to the Assamite sorcerer Ikraam al-Biruni and occasionally poisoning targets for the Black Hand.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Never explain your actions; pursue pleasure after pleasure with apparent randomness, speak in enigmatic non sequiturs about sex, death, and flowers. Caridad's mansion in Xochimilco conceals a bricked-up indoor garden of grow-lamp flowers and drug plants twined through her victims' cadavers, centered on a pomegranate tree she fertilizes with her own vitae.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Donna Fería. Caridad's greatest occult-gardening feats include ghoul bamboo (grows three feet a day, Potence-strong shoots), Cainite asphodel (blooms in a destroyed vampire's remains), and the Pomegranates of Persephone (the fruit or juice casts a mortal into a days-long deathlike torpor; a vampire who feeds on a dosed mortal may fall into a similar torpor, breakable with a Stamina roll, difficulty 6).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
